    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>possibly a trivet, a stand for a pot, kettle or other vessel placed over a fire for cooking or heating something, standing on 3 feet (OED s.v. trefet 1b), but cf. MED (s.v. twibit(e) n.), a two-edged ax | trivet, a stand for a pot, kettle or other vessel placed over a fire for cooking or heating something, standing on 3 feet (OED s.v. trefet 1b)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
